No. It is still part of the same text, therefore part of the same song,
and therefore a seperation is required, otherwise, it sticks to =E2=80=9Cmi=
=E2=80=9D.
It does not MODIFY =E2=80=9Cmi=E2=80=9D, it just means that you have this p=
articular
feeling of freedom towards =E2=80=9Cmi=E2=80=9D.

> d3: Is {noroi} used correctly here?
> d3. .i mi noroi xruti lo sevzi lo purci
> I am never returning myself to a state from the past.
Yes. =E2=80=9Croi=E2=80=9D means =E2=80=9Cn times=E2=80=9D and =E2=80=9Cnor=
oi=E2=80=9D literally means =E2=80=9Czero times=E2=80=9D.
Note this sentence is vague on the time here. I don=E2=80=99t know if
